{
  "document": {
    "format": "deckweft-presentation",
    "schemaVersion": 3,
    "id": "model-comparison-en",
    "title": "GPT-6 Astra and Claude Opus 5.5, side by side",
    "locale": "en",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "cover-title",
        "type": "heading",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Two launch pages.\nOne careful comparison."
      },
      {
        "id": "cover-body",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI) and Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) each published benchmark tables. This deck lines up only the numbers both pages report and says where they differ."
      },
      {
        "id": "cover-note",
        "type": "callout",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "MODEL COMPARISON · FIGURES AS SELF-REPORTED"
      },
      {
        "id": "cover-source",
        "type": "citation",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra"
        ],
        "sourceId": "openai-astra",
        "text": "Vendor launch pages, read 2026-10-23. Not an independent evaluation."
      },
      {
        "id": "bench-title",
        "type": "heading",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Five shared benchmarks.\nNo clean sweep."
      },
      {
        "id": "bench-chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "datasetId": "shared-benchmarks",
        "chartType": "grouped-bar",
        "axis": {
          "policy": "zero"
        },
        "question": "Which model scores higher on each shared benchmark?",
        "takeaway": "Opus 5.5 leads on Terminal-Bench 4.0, FrontierCode and Humanity’s Last Exam; Astra leads on AutomationBench and Terminal-Bench-Science."
      },
      {
        "id": "bench-call",
        "type": "callout",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Opus 5.5 is ahead on three of five; Astra on two."
      },
      {
        "id": "bench-body",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Each pair uses the figure both vendors publish. Effort levels and harnesses differ, so small gaps are not conclusions. Exact values are in the table below the chart."
      },
      {
        "id": "bench-source",
        "type": "citation",
        "sourceIds": [
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "sourceId": "anthropic-opus55",
        "text": "OpenAI and Anthropic launch pages, read 2026-10-23 · unit: %"
      },
      {
        "id": "price-title",
        "type": "heading",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "What it costs\nper million tokens."
      },
      {
        "id": "price-table",
        "type": "table",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "columns": [
          "Price per 1M tokens",
          "GPT-6 Astra",
          "Claude Opus 5.5"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Input",
            "$10",
            "$4"
          ],
          [
            "Output",
            "$50",
            "$20"
          ],
          [
            "Fast mode (input / output)",
            "Up to 2× speed at 2× the standard price",
            "Up to 2.5× speed, $8 / $40"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "price-body",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Anthropic also states that on FrontierCode at default effort Opus 5.5 beats Astra at roughly 20% of the cost per task, and matches it on Terminal-Bench 4.0 at about 40%. Those are Anthropic’s own measurements."
      },
      {
        "id": "price-source",
        "type": "citation",
        "sourceIds": [
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "sourceId": "anthropic-opus55",
        "text": "OpenAI and Anthropic launch pages, read 2026-10-23"
      },
      {
        "id": "lead-title",
        "type": "heading",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Where each page\nstays silent."
      },
      {
        "id": "lead-table",
        "type": "table",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "columns": [
          "Benchmark",
          "GPT-6 Astra",
          "Claude Opus 5.5"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "ARC-AGI-3",
            "99.9%",
            "not reported"
          ],
          [
            "FrontierMath Tier 4 (v2)",
            "97.6%",
            "not reported"
          ],
          [
            "ExploitBench",
            "100.0%",
            "not reported"
          ],
          [
            "GDPval-AA v2.1 (Elo)",
            "1542",
            "1846"
          ],
          [
            "CursorBench 4.0",
            "not reported",
            "57.8%"
          ],
          [
            "OSWorld 2.1 (partial score)",
            "not reported",
            "81.8%"
          ],
          [
            "Chartography (with tools)",
            "not reported",
            "89.0%"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "lead-body",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "A dash is not a loss. Each vendor publishes the benchmarks it leads on or chose to run; a missing cell means that page did not report it."
      },
      {
        "id": "lead-source",
        "type": "citation",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra"
        ],
        "sourceId": "openai-astra",
        "text": "OpenAI and Anthropic launch pages, read 2026-10-23"
      },
      {
        "id": "safe-title",
        "type": "heading",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Safety claims,\nnot a safety score."
      },
      {
        "id": "safe-oa",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra"
        ],
        "text": "OpenAI: on an internal computer-use safety benchmark Astra scores 2.4% (lower is better) against 22.0% for GPT-5.6 Sol; it reports 0% out-of-scope actions where Sol had 48%."
      },
      {
        "id": "safe-an",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Anthropic: Opus 5.5 scores best of any recent Claude model on its automated behavioral audit and attempted to cross containment boundaries about 85% less often than Opus 5; it ties Fable 5.1 for the lowest prompt-injection success rate on a Gray Swan benchmark."
      },
      {
        "id": "safe-call",
        "type": "callout",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Different tests, different baselines. These numbers cannot be compared with each other."
      },
      {
        "id": "safe-source",
        "type": "citation",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra"
        ],
        "sourceId": "openai-astra",
        "text": "OpenAI and Anthropic launch pages, read 2026-10-23"
      },
      {
        "id": "end-title",
        "type": "heading",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "How to read\nthis comparison."
      },
      {
        "id": "end-list",
        "type": "list",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "items": [
          "Every figure is vendor-reported; neither page is an independent evaluation.",
          "Harness, effort level and footnotes differ between pages; compare gaps of a few points with care.",
          "A missing value means the page did not report it, not that the model fails.",
          "Anthropic itself notes that the real-world gap between its models is narrower than benchmark margins suggest."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "end-body",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "sourceIds": [
          "openai-astra",
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "text": "Check the source pages before relying on any number here."
      },
      {
        "id": "end-source",
        "type": "citation",
        "sourceIds": [
          "anthropic-opus55"
        ],
        "sourceId": "anthropic-opus55",
